#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:2 4212cbae5a5249d393421eb005c73c68
msgid "What this is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:4 3253f99ea4a44422b7568d7910c06ea9
msgid ""
"MHVTL is a Linux kernel module and a set of daemons that pretend to be a "
"tape library: a robot that moves cartridges between slots and drives, and"
" drives that write to files on disk. Backup software talks to it exactly "
"as it would to a real library, over SCSI or iSCSI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:9 e20de37ecf3d4fdc824353307a063e1f
msgid ""
"This console is a web interface for it, and a command called ``mhvtl``. "
"They do the same things, because they are the same code: both call one "
"service layer, so neither can do something the other cannot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:14 64a7a6cbf2bc45babeb0e87b7b49f4b4
msgid "What you can do with it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:16 c06b82e5d1b54b0dbea6274e66564a34
msgid ""
"**Create libraries** from the models MHVTL can emulate - an IBM TS3500, "
"an STK SL500, a Quantum Scalar i500 - with the drives and cartridges "
"those models really take."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:19 a1d5d2b6169a4cfaa578b61e8085aa33
msgid ""
"**Fill them with tapes**, one at a time or a barcode run at a time, and "
"put a tape that still has its data back into a library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:21 93000c8e613340a5813432c52c2ce103
msgid "**Drive the robot**: mount, unmount, move a cartridge between slots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:22 47245c7af9b943e292db81a37b2a3736
msgid "**Export a library over iSCSI**, so another machine can back up to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:23 91b2ce32bc7f496382ee88a5b9b4357e
msgid ""
"**Watch a drive while it writes**, which no other tool on the host can do"
" during a backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:25 c98f1dd10fa949e1837f03225beaec15
msgid ""
"**See what the host thinks**: the daemons, the kernel modules, the SCSI "
"devices, the logs, the disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:29 14290b8625a6409e84fe596fb4f2e838
msgid "What it is not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:31 f83c24a6616a47f9ad6f3e2c9ce27c59
msgid ""
"It is not backup software. It gives you a library; what writes to that "
"library is ``tar``, Bacula, NetBackup, Veeam or whatever you already use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:34 79263827292747cfaf1c8b7c8464b6ce
msgid ""
"It does not store your backups anywhere clever: a tape is a directory of "
"files under ``/opt/mhvtl``, and its size is the size you gave it when you"
" made it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:39 0176d4ac0f88418db3de41f303a6bae2
msgid "Why a virtual library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:41 01a063f88e2d4c6ca6983f97642031b0
msgid ""
"Because tape is awkward to test against. A virtual library lets you "
"rehearse a restore, prove a retention policy, train someone, or develop "
"backup software, without a drive, without cartridges, and without waiting"
" for a robot to move anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:47 3e830813b42244cf9ed1cdcac6e8e32f
msgid "The words used here"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:49 8293061ae81d41ed82b0ae3bf0045925
msgid "**Library**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:50 d5dfd99b6ffa44edb597f3d0fb1e9600
msgid ""
"The whole thing: a robot, some drives, and slots to hold cartridges. Has "
"an id - 10, 20, 30 - which is how every command refers to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:53 f07b913e69ea46de93c38c99d720cb2b
msgid "**Drive**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:54 4a754e31bb554a8b84a8cd052076d829
msgid ""
"Writes and reads a cartridge. Has its own id, and belongs to one library."
" MHVTL runs one daemon per drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:57 9832556522a747349fbd2d6793eb519f
msgid "**Slot**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:58 a417196a01704624ac7a4b82ad8c190e
msgid ""
"Where a cartridge sits when it is not in a drive. A library has a fixed "
"number; empty ones are room for tapes added later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:61 d92e1b1174bd41139a9fbc71ef8d2ac2
msgid "**Tape**, or cartridge, or medium"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:62 51e66f33708f4864ad1aa73d00e0f0d9
msgid ""
"Identified by a barcode like ``E01001L8``. The last two characters say "
"which generation it is - ``L8`` is LTO-8 - and that decides which drives "
"can load it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:66 898d152b4b4045498ce1f0059195819d
msgid "**MAP**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:67 d10dada37cdd4ab4a3190c03ede74026
msgid ""
"The mail slot: where a real operator would put a cartridge into the "
"library from outside. MHVTL emulates it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:70 d0c3c38fdc4c451285799953aafa5be0
msgid "**Changer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:71 e5199590a12543a9a87a1962b6b1654c
msgid "The robot, as the kernel sees it: a SCSI device of type ``mediumx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:73 03acd80288834936af606b0baef23f88
msgid "**Profile**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:74 5aa7fc12250a4be5a410b118d1f93322
msgid ""
"A vendor's catalogue: which libraries IBM or STK or Sony make, which "
"drives each of those takes, which cartridges each drive writes, and a "
"sensible default for each. It ships with the console and is never edited."
" Naming one is usually all you have to do - ``mhvtl library create "
"--profile IBM`` picks the rest for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:80 21c3932242e744b489808656d633b543
msgid "**Preset**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/what-it-is.rst:81 7ff69614313f47b792ff0168db053b45
msgid ""
"A configuration *you* built from a profile and gave a name to, so the "
"same library can be built again without retyping it. Eleven ship as "
"examples, one for each vendor. The difference from a profile is who owns "
"it: a profile is what a vendor makes and cannot be changed, a preset is a"
" set of choices made from one and is yours to edit, rename or delete. See"
" :doc:`../libraries/profiles-and-presets`."
msgstr ""

